Page 515 rocháda: Found match for regex: =
Page 515 rocháda: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|cs|de|Rochade||castling}}, from {{der|cs|gmh|roch||rook}}, from {{der|cs|fa|رخ|tr=rox|t=war elephant}}.<ref name="Rejzek"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{cs-IPA|rošáda}}
* {{rhymes|cs|aːda|s=3}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|ro|chá|da}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|f}}

# {{lb|cs|obsolete|chess}} {{alternative form of|cs|rošáda}} {{gloss|[[castling]]}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=1986|author=Jiří Veselý|title=Jak hrát šachy?|chapter=Rocháda|page=17|publisher=Olympia|location=Praha|url= |isbn= |passage=Hráč při '''rochádě''' uchopí vlastního krále, přesune ho o dvě pole směrem k vlastní věži, pak vezme onu věž a přeskočí vlastního krále tak, že ji postaví do králova těsného sousedství na téže řadě.|translation=When performing castling, a player takes his own king, moves it two squares towards his own rook, than takes the rook and jumps over his own king in such a way, that he puts it to the king's close neighbourhood on the same row.}}

====Usage notes====
The expression ''rocháda'' should be pronounced {{IPAchar|/ˈroxaːda/}}, but it mistakenly acquired also [[w:French language|French]] pronunciation with the letter "''{{l|cs|ch}}''" pronounced as {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} (especially among non-professional chess players), which later (in 1950's) lead also to the change of spelling with the letter "''š''" (''{{l|cs|rošáda}}'').<ref name="Rejzek"/><ref name="CTC"/><ref name="Nase rec"/>

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|f}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|cs|rochovat|malá rocháda|velká rocháda}}

