===Etymology===
Akin to surnames {{m|cs|Vokurka}}, {{m|cs|Vogurka}}, {{cog|zlw-ocs|oharek}} (since c. 1410), {{cog|sk|uhorka}}, {{cog|zlw-opl|ogurek}} (since 1394), {{cog|pl|ogórek}}, all perhaps from {{der|cs|gkm|ἀγγούριον}} or a related form. Derivative ''wokurko[we]'' attested around mid-15th century.

