Page 2143 mechovka: Found match for regex: =
Page 2143 mechovka: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|cs|mech|ovka}}.
* {{sense|Clitopilus}} First used by Czech botanist Jan Bezděk in 1901.<ref name="Bezděk"/> The name probably refers to the fact that the fungus often grows in moss ({{cog|cs|mech}}).
* {{sense|moss animal}} {{clq|cs|mul|Bryozoa}}, from {{der|cs|grc|βρύον||moss}} + {{m|grc|ζῷα}}, which is a plural of {{m|grc|ζῷον||animal}}. It refers to the fact that colonies of some species of these animals resemble [[moss]] ({{cog|cs|mech}}).<ref name="Živa"/>
* {{sense|Rosa × centifolia var. muscosa}} Refers to the moss-like surface of the [[sepal]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|cs|ofka|s=3}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|me|chov|ka}}

===Noun===
[[File:Clitopilus prunulus, Strouds Run State Park 6.jpg|thumbnail|[[mechovka obecná]] ({{taxlink|Clitopilus prunulus|species|ver=181026}})]]
[[File:Cristatella mucedo 2014 11 10 a14.JPG|thumbnail|[[mechovka hadovitá]] ({{taxlink|Cristatella mucedo|species|ver=181026}}), a representative of [[Bryozoa]]]]
[[File:BotMag2(69).jpg|thumbnail|mechovka, [[mechová růže]] ({{taxlink|Rosa centifolia var. muscosa|variety|Rosa&nbsp;× centifolia ''var''.&nbsp;muscosa}})]]
{{cs-noun|f}}

# {{taxlink|Clitopilus|genus|ver=181026}} {{gloss|genus of [[fungi]] in the [[family]] {{taxlink|Entolomataceae|family|ver=181026}}}}
# [[moss animal]], [[bryozoan]], a representative of the [[phylum]] [[Bryozoa]]
# {{taxlink|Rosa × centifolia|nothospecies|ver=181026}} var. ''muscosa'' {{gloss|a kind of a [[hybrid]] [[rose]]}}
#: {{syn|cs|mechová růže}}

====Usage notes====
Czech names of [[Bryozoa]] and some of its subgroups are often used ambiguously. While some authors use the name {{m|cs|mechovky}} for the whole phylum Bryozoa,<ref name="CBG"/> others call them {{m|cs|mechovci}}, leaving the name ''mechovky'' only for its class [[Phylactolaemata]].<ref name="BioLib1"/> Then singular ''mechovka'' refers to any representative of the groups. Besides this, the name ''mechovka'' is also used for many (but not all) of the genera from various classes of the phylum Bryozoa.<ref name="BioLib2"/>

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|f}}

====Hypernyms====
* {{sense|genus Clitopilus}} {{l|cs|houby}}&nbsp;– kingdom; {{l|cs|stopkovýtrusné}}&nbsp;– division; {{l|cs|rouškaté}}&nbsp;– class; {{l|cs|pečárkotvaré}}&nbsp;– order; {{l|cs|závojenkovité}}&nbsp;– family
* {{sense|phylum Bryozoa}} {{l|cs|živočichové}}&nbsp;– kingdom; {{l|cs|prvoústí}}&nbsp;– clade
* {{sense|species Rosa × centifolia var. muscosa}} {{l|cs|rostliny}}&nbsp;– kingdom; {{l|cs|vyšší rostliny}}&nbsp;– subkingdom; {{l|cs|krytosemenné}}&nbsp;– clade; {{l|cs|vyšší dvouděložné}}&nbsp;– clade; {{l|cs|růžotvaré}}&nbsp;– order; {{l|cs|růžovité}}&nbsp;– family; {{l|cs|růže}}&nbsp;– genus; {{l|cs|růže stolistá}}&nbsp;– species

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|genus Clitopilus}} {{l|cs|mechovka běloučká}}, {{l|cs|mechovka Hobsonova}}, {{l|cs|mechovka obecná}}, {{l|cs|mechovka prostřední}}

====Related terms====
{{col-auto|cs|mech|mecháček|mechovec|mechový|omšelý}}

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Bezděk">{{cite-book|author=Jan Bezděk|date=1901|title=Houby jedlé a jim podobné jedovaté|volume=1|location=Praha|publisher=|page=}}</ref>
<ref name="Živa">Irena Šetlíková; et al. (2005). "Nepůvodní druh mechovky na Třeboňsku". Živa. No. 4 (Academia). p. 172. Retrieved 2016-01-09.</ref>
<ref name="CBG">[http://www.kbi.zcu.cz/OB/veda/paleontologie/zoopaleontologie/mechovky/index.php "Kmen Bryozoa – mechovky"]. Západočeská univerzita v Plzni: Centrum biologie, geověd a envigogiky. Retrieved 2016-01-08.</ref>
<ref name="BioLib1">[http://www.biolib.cz/cz/taxonsubtaxa/id20141/ "třída: mechovky: Phylactolaemata"]. BioLib.cz. Retrieved 2016-01-08.</ref>
<ref name="BioLib2">[http://www.biolib.cz/cz/formsearch/?action=execute&searcharea=1&string=mechovka "nalezené národní názvy"]. BioLib.cz. Retrieved 2016-01-08.</ref>
</references>

