===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|cs|oːla|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|štó|la}}

===Etymology 1===
{{wikipedia|lang=cs}}
{{inh+|cs|zlw-ocs|štóla}}, from {{der|cs|la|stola||stola}}, from {{der|cs|grc|στολή}}, which is from {{der|cs|grc|στέλλω}}.<ref name="Rejzek">{{R:cs:Rejzek 2015|štóla|705}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{cs-noun|f}}

# {{senseid|cs|stole}}[[stole]] {{gloss|priest's garment, a stripe of cloth worn around the neck and shoulders}} {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2013 |author=Petra Pachlová |title=Ztracené duše |page=123–124 |publisher=Domino |location=Ostrava |url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=idhCAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA124&dq=%22%C5%A1t%C3%B3la%22#v=onepage&q=%22%C5%A1t%C3%B3la%22&f=false |isbn=978-80-7303-945-5 |original=Lost Souls |by=Lisa Jackson |passage=Seděl se založenými rukama oblečený do bílého kněžského roucha, přes které mu splývala zlatem zdobená '''štóla'''. |translation=He was sitting with folded arms, wearing a white vestment, across which a stole decorated with gold was hanging.}}
# [[stole]] {{gloss|ladie's scarf-like garment, often made of fur}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2013 |author=Jana Montorio Doležalová |title=Alchymie věčnosti |page=129 |publisher=Cooboo |location=Praha |url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=MmAnCwAAQBAJ&pg=PA129&dq=%22%C5%A1t%C3%B3ly%22#v=onepage&q=%22%C5%A1t%C3%B3ly%22&f=false |isbn=978-80-7447-252-7 |original=The alchemy of forever |by=Avery Williams |passage=Zabořila jsem nos do kožešinové štóly, jak jsem se chvěla zimou. |translation=I was shivering from cold, so I burried my nose into the fur stole.}}
# [[payment]] given to Christian [[priest]]s for various liturgical acts such as weddings or funerals
#* {{quote-journal|cs|author=|editor=|title=|journal=Hlídka |url=https://books.google.cz/books?hl=cs&id=tjjOsNRdozQC&dq=%C5%A1t%C3%B3la|year=1921 |volume=38 |issue=|page=197|passage=Za války husité mluvili s rozhořčením anebo hrubým posměchem i o takových štolových poplatcích, které byly pro chudé kněze nevyhnutelné; '''štóla''' dle husitské zásady byla svatokupectvím. |translation=During the war Hussites spoke with indignation or with harsch ridicule about the payments for liturgical acts, which were inevitable for poor priests; '''payment for a liturgical act''' was a simony according to Hussite principles.}}

