Page 4830 delta: -------- begin text --------
{{enum|cs|gama|epsilon|Greek letter|Δδ}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|cs|grc|δέλτα}}, which is probably of {{l|en|Semitic}} origin.<ref name="Rejzek"/>

====Noun====
{{cs-noun|n|indecl=1}}

# {{l|en|delta|Delta}} {{gloss|Greek letter Δ}}
# {{lb|cs|physics}} kind of [[ray]]s consisting of secondary electrons with enough [[energy]] to escape a significant distance away from the primary [[radiation]] [[beam]] and produce further [[ionization]] {{gloss|[[delta ray]]}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|cs|deltový}}

====Adjective====
{{cs-adj|indecl=1}}

# having the shape of the Greek letter {{lang|el|[[Δ]]}}
#: {{coi|cs|delta křídlo|delta wing}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|cs|grc|δέλτα}}. Originally used for the {{l|en|delta}} of the {{l|en|Nile}}, because its {{l|en|forked}} shape resembled the Greek letter {{lang|el|[[Δ]]}}. The word is probably of {{l|en|Semitic}} origin.<ref name="Rejzek"/>

====Noun====
{{cs-noun|f}}

# {{lb|cs|geography}} {{l|en|delta}} {{gloss|forked mouth of a river}}

=====Declension=====
{{cs-ndecl|f}}

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Rejzek">{{R:cs:Rejzek 2015|delta|137}}</ref>
</references>

