===Etymology===
{{inh+|cs|sla-pro|*bъlbъ}}, from {{inh|cs|ine-pro|*stl̥b-}}, an {{glossary|ablaut}} variant of {{m|ine-pro|*stelb||post, pole, jamb}} (whence also {{m|lv|stilbs}}, [[q.v.]]), from {{m|ine-pro|*stel-||to put in a standing position, to erect; standing, immobile, stiff}} with an extra ''b''. The semantic evolution was probably: “motionless, stiff” > “surprised, stunned” > “stupid”. Cognates include {{cog|sga|borb|t=foolish, silly}}, {{cog|lv|stulbs|t=stupid, dumb}} and {{cog|la|stultus|t=foolish, fatuous}}.

===Pronunciation===
