{{wp|lang=cs}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|cs|zlw-ocs|hrad}}, from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*gȏrdъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|hrad}}
* {{rhymes|cs|at|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-in}}

# [[castle]]

====Usage notes====
* The word '''''hrad''''' is used for castles whose main function seems to be [[defence]], while {{m|cs|zámek}} is used for those whose main function seems to be [[ostentation]]. For example, the [[w:Castles and Town Walls of King Edward in Gwynedd|castles of King Edward in Gwynedd]] are ''hrady'', while the [[w:Châteaux of the Loire Valley|Loire Valley castles]] are ''zámky''. The difference can be subjective, so that for example [[w:Windsor Castle|Windsor Castle]] can be called by either term by different speakers.

====Declension====
