Page 7987 letargie: Found match for regex: {
Page 7987 letargie: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=cs}}

===Etymology===
From late {{der|cs|la|lēthargia}}, from {{der|cs|grc|ληθαργία||drowsiness}}, from {{m|grc|λήθαργος||forgetful, lethargic}}. This is a compound of {{m|grc|λήθη||oblivion}} and {{m|grc|ἀργός||idle}}, which consists of negative prefix {{m|grc|ἀ-}} and noun {{m|grc|ἔργον||deed, work}}.
<ref name="Rejzek"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|cs|ɪjɛ|s=4}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|le|tar|gie}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|f}}

# {{lb|cs|pathology}} [[lethargy|Lethargy]] {{gloss|pathological drowsiness}} {{defdate|19th c.}}
# {{lb|cs|psychology}} [[lethargy|Lethargy]] {{gloss|apathy, lack of emotions and interest}}
# {{lb|cs|nuclear physics}} [[lethargy|Lethargy]] {{gloss|quantity characterizing the rate of decelaration of neutrons}}

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|f}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|cs|letargický}}

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Rejzek">{{R:cs:Rejzek 2015|letargie|375}}</ref>
</references>

===Further reading===
* {{R:cs:PSJC}}
* {{R:cs:SSJC}}
* {{R:cs:IJP}}

{{C|cs|Diseases|Medical signs and symptoms}}

