Page 8503 puzzle: Found match for regex: =
Page 8503 puzzle: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|cs|en|puzzle}}.<ref>{{R:cs:Rejzek 2007}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA|pazl}}
* {{q|nonstandard|hyperforeign}} {{cs-IPA|pucle}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-in|g2=n|g3=f}}

# [[jigsaw puzzle]]

====Usage notes====
Also used as an indeclinable noun of various genders, most often neuter.<ref>[http://prirucka.ujc.cas.cz/?slovo=puzzle ''puzzle'' in Internetová jazyková příručka], Institute of the Czech Language of the Academy of Sciences of the Czech Republic</ref>

Although the standard pronunciation of this word, which has been borrowed from English, is {{IPAchar|/ˈpazl̩/|lang=cs}}, another common informal pronunciation is {{IPAchar|/ˈput͡sle/|lang=cs}}, which is a {{l|en|hyperforeignism}}, trying to apply either Italian (as in {{m|it|pizza}}) or more probably German pronunciation rules.<ref>{{R:cs:Nase rec|author=|title=Z dopisů jazykové poradně|url=http://nase-rec.ujc.cas.cz/archiv.php?art=7538|year=1999|volume=82|issue=5}}</ref> However, both Italian and German pronunciation of the word ''puzzle'' is different.

====Declension====
''when masculine:''
{{cs-ndecl|m.foreign}}
''Indeclinable when neuter or feminine.''

===References===
<references />

{{cln|cs|indeclinable nouns|hyperforeign terms}}

