===Etymology===
{{bor+|cs|sk|batoh}} with the same meaning.<ref name="machek" /><ref name="rejzek" /> In old Czech, ''batoh'' had a different meaning (“whip, stick”), inherited from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*batogъ}}.<ref name="rejzek" /> It is unclear whether the word changed meaning (possibly via “a stick to carry baggage”, and “baggage carried using a stick”) or the modern usage is a new derivation (Machek’s theory of derivation from {{noncog|de|Weidtasche||hunter’s bag}}<ref name="machek">{{R:cs:Machek 1968|batoh|48}}</ref> is considered implausible by Rejzek).<ref name="rejzek">{{R:cs:Rejzek 2015||77}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
