===Etymology===
From {{suffix|cs|hák|ek}}. The diminutive form of {{m|cs|hák||hook}}; compare the {{cog|de|Häkchen}}. More information is in the [[#English|'Etymology' subsection of 'English' section]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{audio|cs|Cs-háček.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-in}}

# {{diminutive of|cs|hák}}; little [[hook]]
# [[fishhook]]
# {{lb|cs|linguistics}} {{l|en|háček}} {{gloss|diacritic}}
# [[catch]], [[snag]] {{gloss|a concealed difficulty, especially in a deal or negotiation}}
# {{lb|cs|canoeing}} [[bow]]
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2005|author=Martin Patřičný|title=Dřevo krásných stromů|page=20|publisher=Grada Publishing|location=Praha|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=wLi-AgAAQBAJ&pg=PA20|isbn=978-80-247-6992-9|passage=Mně se ta holka nijak zvlášť nelíbila, ale když jsem ji měl na háčku (pro nevodáky vpředu v kanoi), tak byla dobrá.|translation=I didn't like the girl very much, but when she was at the bow (for non-canoeists the front of the canoe), she was good.}}

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|m}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|en|háček}}
* {{desc|ja|ハーチェク|tr=hācheku}}
* {{desc|ru|га́чек}}

====See also====
* {{l|cs|udice}}
* {{l|cs|čárka}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-an}}

# {{lb|cs|canoeing}} [[bow paddler]]
#: {{ant|cs|zadák|kormidelník}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2007|author=Jakub Turek|coauthors=et al|title=Outdoorový průvodce - Český ráj: 31 tipů, kam na výlet|page=84|publisher=Grada Publishing|location=Praha|url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=18haAgAAQBAJ&pg=PA84#v=onepage&q&f=false|isbn=978-80-247-2022-7|passage=Kormidelník musí ovládat základní záběry, háček může být bez větších zkušeností.|translation=The stern paddler has to know the basic strokes, the bow paddler doesn't need to have much experience.}}

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|m.an}}

