Page 10906 lošák: Found match for regex: [
Page 10906 lošák: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Sarcodon imbricatus T64.jpg|thumbnail|[[lošák jelení]] ({{taxlink|Sarcodon imbricatus|species}})]]

===Etymology===
{{bor+|cs|pl|łosiak}}, from {{m|pl|łoś||elk}}.<ref name="Machek"/> Introduced into [[w:Czech language|Czech]] by the botanist [[w:Jan Svatopluk Presl|Jan Svatopluk Presl]] in 1846.<ref name="Presl"/> The name probably reflects the colour of some of the representatives of these mushrooms, such as {{taxlinknew|Sarcodon imbricatus|species|noshow=1}} ({{m+|cs|lošák jelení}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|cs|ʃaːk|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|lo|šák}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-in}}

# certain [[tooth fungus|tooth fungi]]:
## {{taxlink|Hydnum|genus}} {{gloss|[[genus]] of [[fungus|fungi]] in the family {{taxlink|Hydnaceae|family|ver=190803}}}} {{defdate|19th c.}}
##: {{syn|cs|lišák}}
## {{taxlink|Sarcodon|genus}} {{gloss|[[genus]] of [[fungus|fungi]] in the family {{taxlink|Bankeraceae|family|ver=190803}}}}

====Usage notes====
Although the word ''lošák'' should be declined as masculine inanimate, in practical colloquial usage the animate declension also sometimes appears.<ref name="Nase rec"/>

The species belonging to the genera ''Hydnum'' and ''Sarcodon'' were originally classified as one genus (''Hydnum''), called ''lošák'' in Czech. After the two genera split and received different scientific names, the Czech name ''lošák'' has remained in usage for both of them, although many Czech mycologists have preferred calling the fungi of the genus ''Hydnum'' {{m|cs|lišák}}, reserving the name ''lošák'' for the fungi of the genus ''Sarcodon''.

====Declension====
''inanimate:''
{{cs-ndecl|m}}
''animate:''
{{cs-ndecl|m.an}}

====Hypernyms====
* {{sense|genus Hydnum}} {{l|cs|houby}}&nbsp;– kingdom; {{l|cs|stopkovýtrusné}}&nbsp;– division; {{l|cs|rouškaté}}&nbsp;– class; {{l|cs|liškotvaré}}&nbsp;– order; {{l|cs|lišákovité}}&nbsp;– family
* {{sense|genus Sarcodon}} {{l|cs|houby}}&nbsp;– kingdom; {{l|cs|stopkovýtrusné}}&nbsp;– division; {{l|cs|rouškaté}}&nbsp;– class; {{l|cs|plesňákotvaré}}&nbsp;– order; {{l|cs|bělozubovité}}&nbsp;– family

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|genus Hydnum}} {{l|cs|lišák bělavý}}, {{l|cs|lišák ryšavý}}, {{l|cs|lišák zprohýbaný}}&nbsp;– species
* {{sense|genus Sarcodon}} {{l|cs|lošák balzámový}}, {{l|cs|lošák fialový}}, {{l|cs|lošák finský}}, {{l|cs|lošák hladký}}, {{l|cs|lošák hořký}}, {{l|cs|lošák jelení}}, {{l|cs|lošák Lundellův}}, {{l|cs|lošák sivonohý}}, {{l|cs|lošák šupinatý}}&nbsp;– species

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|cs|lošáček|lošákovec}}

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Presl">"[https://books.google.cz/books?id=UsxLAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1919#v=onepage&q&f=false lošák]" in Jan Swatopluk Presl, Wšeobecný rostlinopis, Kronbergr a Řiwnáč, 1846, page 1919.</ref>
<ref name="Machek">"lošák" in Václav Machek, Etymologický slovník jazyka českého, Academia, 1968, page 340.</ref>
<ref name="Nase rec">{{R:cs:Nase rec|author=|title=Z našich časopisů|url=http://nase-rec.ujc.cas.cz/archiv.php?art=3951|year=1946|volume=30|issue=2–3}}</ref>
</references>

