# [[Indian]], [[Amerindian]], [[Native American]] {{gloss|a member of one of the indigenous peoples of the Americas}}

=====Declension=====
{{cs-ndecl|m.an}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|cs|indiánka|indiánský}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|cs|Ind}}

===Etymology 2===
From [[#Etymology 1|indián (1)]], probably because of the color of the chocolate topping; in use by the end of the 19th century.<ref>{{R:cs:Rejzek 2007|indiánek}}</ref> According to Vladimír Šmilauer, the name was used in the ''Kuchařská kniha domácnosti'' cookbook from 1890.<ref>{{R:cs:Machek 1968|indián(ek)}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{cs-noun|m-an|g2=m-in}}

# a type of chocolate-coated dessert filled with [[meringue]]
#: {{syn|cs|indiánek}}

=====Declension=====
{{cs-ndecl|((m,m.an))}}

===References===
<references />

