{{wp|lang=cs}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|cs|zlw-ocs|ucho}}, from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*uxo}}, from {{inh|cs|ine-bsl-pro|*aušis}}, from {{inh|cs|ine-pro|*h₂ṓws}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{audio|cs|Cs-ucho.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|n}}

# [[ear]] {{q|of a human, animal, puppet, humanoid robot, etc.}}
#: {{uxi|cs|[[v|V ]] '''uších''' [[se]] [[jí]] [[třpytily]] [[briliantový|briliantové]] [[náušnice]].|Brilliant earrings glittered at her '''ears'''.}}
#: {{uxi|cs|[[být]] [[jedno]] '''ucho'''.|to be all '''ears'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* The irregular plural forms originated as the dual in Old Czech, while the regular plural forms below were the Old Czech plural. But the plurals are now simply split by meaning, no matter how many objects are being talked about.

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|((n.sg,uši<n.pl.decllemma:uší.inspl:ušima>))}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|n}}

# anything resembling an [[ear]]:
## [[handle]] {{q|of a pot, jug, garbage can, shopping bag, trophy, etc.}}
## [[eye]] {{q|of a needle}}
## [[ear]] [[flap]] {{q|on a hat}}
## {{lb|cs|glassblowing}} [[protrusion]] at the [[edge]] of a [[plate]] of [[glass]]
## {{n-g|used in folk names of various plants}}, e.g.:
### {{coi|cs|babí ucho|lit=granny's ear|t=greater plaintain (''[[Plantago major]]'')}}
