===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|cs|zlw-ocs|dno}}, from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*dъno}}, {{m|sla-pro|*dbъno||bottom}}, which is probably from {{der|cs|ine-pro|*dʰub-}} or {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeub-}} ({{m|ine-pro|*dʰewb-}}). Cognates are e. g. {{cog|lt|dùgnas||bottom}}, {{cog|lv|dubens||bottom}}, {{cog|de|Tief||deep}} and {{cog|en|deep}}. Transposition from {{cog|ine-pro|*bʰudʰ-}} to {{m|ine-pro|*dʰubʰ-}} is also possible. Cognates derived from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰudʰ-}} include {{cog|de|Boden}}, {{cog|la|fundus}} (compare {{cog|cs|fond}}), {{cog|grc|πυθμήν}}, {{cog|xcl|բուն}}, {{cog|sa|बुध्न}} {{gloss|all meaning "bottom", "base"}}.<ref name="Rejzek"/>

