Page 18265 olomoucké syrečky: Found match for regex: {
Page 18265 olomoucké syrečky: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=cs}}
[[File:Olomoucké tvarůžky (1).jpg|thumb|''olomoucké syrečky'']]

===Etymology===
The noun {{m|cs|syrečky}} is a plural form of {{m|cs|syreček}}, which is a {{gloss|diminutive}} of {{m|cs|sýr||cheese}}. The adjective {{m|cs|olomoucké}} is a masculine plural nominative of {{m|cs|olomoucký||from Olomouc}} and refers to the fact that the cheese has been traditionally produced in the surroundings of the city of {{w|Olomouc}} and in the past used to be sold especially in Olomouc markets.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-in-p|head=[[olomoucký|olomoucké]] [[syreček|syrečky]]}}

# [[Olomouc cheese]] {{gloss|a kind of ripened soft cheese, characteristic with its strong scent, distinctive pungent taste and yellowish colour, nowadays made in the town of {{w|Loštice}}, the Czech Republic}}
#: {{syn|cs|homolky<q:obsolete>|;|olomoucké tvarůžky|;|syrečky|;|tvargle<q:informal>|;|tvarůžky}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2014 |author=Valenta Milan |title=Muřinoh a Krchomilka |page=62 |publisher=Albatros |location=Praha |pageurl=https://books.google.cz/books?id=nQgnCwAAQBAJ&pg=PA62&dq=%22olomouck%C3%A9+syre%C4%8Dky%22#v=onepage&q=%22olomouck%C3%A9%20syre%C4%8Dky%22&f=false |isbn=978-80-00-03664-9 |passage=Tomuto rozhodnutí předcházela úvaha o založení rodiny, uzrálá v něm do voňava jako '''olomoucké syrečky''', které si s oblibou dopřával k pozdní snídani. |translation=}}

====Usage notes====
In {{w|Moravia}} the term {{m|cs|olomoucké tvarůžky}} or shortly {{m|cs|tvarůžky}} prevails, while in {{w|Bohemia}} they are usually called ''olomoucké syrečky'' or shortly {{m|cs|syrečky}}.

The term is usually used only in the plural form ''olomoucké syrečky'', although the singular form {{m|cs|olomoucký syreček}} occasionally occurs.

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|[[olomoucký|olomoucké]]<+> [[syreček|syrečky]]<m.pl>}}

====Related terms====
{{col-auto|cs|sýr|sýrový|syreček|syrečkový|syrečkárna}}

====Further reading====
* {{comcatlite|Olomoucké tvarůžky|olomoucké syrečky}}

{{cln|cs|terms derived from toponyms}}
{{C|cs|Cheeses|Olomouc}}
