{{wikipedia|lang=cs|newspeak|novořeč}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|cs|nový|-o-|řeč}}. {{calque|cs|en|newspeak}}, from {{m|en|Newspeak}}, from {{compound|en|new|speak|nocat=1}}, coined by {{w|George Orwell}} in the 1949 novel ''{{w|Nineteen Eighty-Four}}''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|cs|or̝ɛtʃ|r̝ɛtʃ|s=3}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|no|vo|řeč}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|f}}

# [[newspeak]] {{defdate|since 20th c.}}
#: {{syn|cs|newspeak}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2004 |author=Václav Burian |title=Masłowská, Dorota: Červená a bílá |chapter=Doslov |page= |publisher=Odeon |location=Praha| url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=a4JIDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA199&dq=novo%C5%99e%C4%8D#v=onepage&q=novo%C5%99e%C4%8D&f=false |isbn= |passage={{...}}komunistická '''novořeč''' stírala individuální vlastnosti uživatele a znemožňovala ocenit jeho skutečnou hloupost či inteligenci. |translation={{...}}communistic '''newspeak''' reduced individual qualities of its users and made impossible to acknowledge their stupidity or intelligence.}}

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|f.istem}}

{{cln|cs|terms derived from Nineteen Eighty-Four}}
{{C|cs|Language}}
