Page 18791 kostrč: Found match for regex: {
Page 18791 kostrč: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=cs}}
{{was fwotd|cs|2017|April|8}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|cs|sla-pro|*kostrьcь}} which is from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*kostra||skeleton}}. This probably comes from several intermingling sources: from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*kostr-}}, {{m|sla-pro|*kostь||bone}} and at the same time the root {{m|sla-pro|*kes-}}, which is from {{der|cs|ine-pro|*kes-||to scratch}}. The present [[w:Czech language|Czech]] form ''kostrč'' was probably also influenced by the word {{m|cs|trčet||stick out}}.<ref>{{R:cs:Rejzek 2015|kostrč|337}}</ref> Compare {{m|cs|kost}}, {{m|cs|kostra}} and {{m|cs|kostrbatý}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|ko|s|trč}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|f}}

# [[tailbone]], [[coccyx]] {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#: {{syn|cs|kostřec|q=obsolete}}
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2009 |author=Ivan Dylevský |title=Speciální kineziologie |page=75 |publisher=Grada Publishing |location=Praha |url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=bl2vEYBC9qYC&pg=PA75#v=onepage&q&f=false |isbn=978-80-247-1648-0 |passage='''Kostrč''' je malá trojúhelníkovitá kost tvořící zakončení páteře. |translation=The '''tailbone''' is a small triangular bone forming an end of the spine.}}

====Declension====
{{cs-ndecl|f}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|cs|kostrční}}

====Related terms====
{{col-auto|cs|kost|kostní|kostra|kosterní|kostroun|kostrový|kostřička|kůstka}}

===References===
<references/>

