===Etymology 1===
From {{m|cs||manželé}}, plural of {{m|cs|manžel||husband}} (see [[#Etymology 2|Etymology 2]] below).

====Noun====
{{cs-noun|m-an-p}}

# {{lb|cs|plurale tantum}} [[married couple]], [[husband and wife]]
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=2014 |author=Marek Mahler |title=Vyhnanci z Ráje |chapter= |page= |publisher=Plot |location= |url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=82UbBAAAQBAJ&pg=PT205&dq=man%C5%BEel%C3%A9#v=onepage&q=man%C5%BEel%C3%A9&f=false |isbn=978-80-7428-229-4 |passage=Přesvědčení komunisté, '''manželé''' Rosenbergovi, vynášeli informace o americkém jaderném výzkumu Sovětskému svazu. |translation=Convinced communists '''husband and wife''' Julius and Ethel Rosenberg leaked the information of the American nuclear research to the Soviet Union.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The word usually refers to [[husband and wife]] married to each other, although it can refer also to partners in a male [[gay marriage]] (but not in a [[lesbian]] marriage).

