===Etymology===
{{inh+|cs|sla-pro|*dǫbъ||oak}}, which has not been explained yet. It could be an innovation appearing because of a [[taboo]] (since oak was a sacred tree). There are some attempts to connect it with e.g. {{cog|ine-pro|*dem-||build}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeu-bʰ-||dark}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeu-b-||deep}} or {{m|ine-pro|*dʰembʰ||beat}}.<ref name="Rejzek"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|dou|bí}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|n}} {{lb|cs|collective|singulare tantum}}

# [[oak]] vegetation
# snarl of oak branches

