Page 20103 lošák jelení: Found match for regex: [
Page 20103 lošák jelení: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Habichtspilz-Sarcodon-imbricatus.jpg|thumbnail|lošák jelení<br/>({{taxlink|Sarcodon imbricatus|species|noshow=1}})]]

===Etymology===
{{coined|cs|Jan Svatopluk Presl}} in 1846.<ref name="Presl"/> The noun {{m|cs|lošák||Sarcodon}}, which is from {{der|cs|pl|łosiak}}, from {{m|pl|łoś||elk}},<ref name="Machek"/> probably refers to the colour of the mushroom, somewhat resembling the colour of [[elk]]. At the same time the adjective {{m|cs|jelení||deer-like}} reminds the colour of a [[deer]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{cs-noun|m-in|g2=m-an}}

# {{taxlink|Sarcodon imbricatus|species|noshow=1}} {{qualifier|''species of [[fungi]] in the family {{taxlink|Bankeraceae|family|noshow=1}}''}} {{defdate|19th c.}}
#: {{syn|cs|jelenice}}

====Usage notes====
* Although the word ''lošák'' should be declined as masculine inanimate, in practical colloquial usage the animate declension also sometimes appears.<ref name="Nase rec">{{R:cs:Nase rec|author=|title=Z našich časopisů|url=http://nase-rec.ujc.cas.cz/archiv.php?art=3951|year=1946|volume=30|issue=2–3}}</ref>

====Declension====
''when inanimate:''
{{cs-ndecl|lošák<m> jelení<+>}}
''when animate:''
{{cs-ndecl|lošák<m.an> jelení<+>}}

====Hypernyms====
* {{sense|species}} {{l|cs|houby}}&nbsp;– kingdom; {{l|cs|stopkovýtrusné}}&nbsp;– division; {{l|cs|rouškaté}}&nbsp;– class; {{l|cs|plesňákotvaré}}&nbsp;– order; {{l|cs|bělozubovité}}&nbsp;– family; {{l|cs|lošák}}&nbsp;– genus

===References===
<references>
<ref name="Presl">"[https://books.google.cz/books?id=UsxLAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1919#v=onepage&q&f=false lošák]" in Jan Swatopluk Presl, Wšeobecný rostlinopis, Kronbergr a Řiwnáč, 1846, page 1919.</ref>
<ref name="Machek">"lošák" in Václav Machek, Etymologický slovník jazyka českého, Academia, 1968, page 340.</ref>
</references>

===Further reading===
* {{R:cs:Myko|Sarcodon-imbricatus}}
* {{pedia|lang=cs}}
* {{comcatlite|i=1|Sarcodon imbricatus}}
* {{specieslite|Bankeraceae}}

